    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but pruning is different. pruning is intentional. it's done to save the rest of the tree. when i look at them, i don't see a tree that needs grace, i just see a legacy that's getting heavier and uglier every time i breathe. i feel like the only way to actually honor what they did is to stop being the thing that's dragging it down.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
